# ---- ML artifacts (added 2026-08-16) --------------------------------------
# Training output, datasets, and model weights: large, regenerable or
# re-downloadable, and never belongs in git. Source and configs stay tracked.
# Build outputs. Model weights are never committed (they are large and regenerable),
# but the per-job run records ARE published: PAPER section 10 lists them as required
# reproduction artifacts, and excluding them wholesale was gap B3. metrics.jsonl +
# config.json across all of nanolab/out is ~16 MB; the 542 MB is .pt checkpoints.
# NOTE: these patterns must match at any depth. A bare `out/**` contains a slash,
# so git anchors it to the repo root and every nested out/ (Rust_MLKit/.../out,
# nanolab/out) silently becomes tracked -- that added 1862 + 376 files here.
**/out/**
!**/out/**/
!**/out/**/metrics.jsonl
!**/out/**/config.json
!**/out/**/queue.json
!**/out/**/recipe.json
!**/out/**/ledger.json
!**/out/**/summary.json
# Added 2026-08-29. The recall probe (paper section 6.8) writes one ledger per suite
# rather than one metrics.jsonl per run, and the end-of-schedule losses recovered
# from checkpoints are the only surviving record for suites whose weights are gone
# (section 7.4 item 11). Section 10 states both are published; these rules make that true.
!**/out/**/runs.jsonl
!**/out/**/final_val.json
!**/out/final_vals_recovered.json
*.pt
models/
.artifacts/
data/
**/data/
checkpoints/
**/checkpoints/
ema_weights/
**/ema_weights/

